# Gradient multi-start fixture (#386 follow-up).
# Two independent first-order decays observed as their SUM:
#   Stot(t) = A*exp(-k1*t) + B*exp(-k2*t).
# With A == B the sum-of-squares surface in (k1, k2) is symmetric under k1<->k2,
# so the diagonal k1 == k2 (where the model collapses to a single exponential
# (A+B)*exp(-k*t)) is an invariant manifold of the gradient flow: a single start
# from the box center (k1 == k2) is trapped at the best single-exponential fit,
# a strict non-global minimum, while an off-diagonal start recovers the true,
# well-separated rates. The multimodal target that makes local multi-start's win
# visible. k1 / k2 are bare parameter ids (bind by id to the rate, parameter axis).
begin model

begin parameters
  A   50
  B   50
  k1  0.1
  k2  2.0
end parameters

begin molecule types
  P()
  Q()
end molecule types

begin seed species
  P()  A
  Q()  B
end seed species

begin observables
  Molecules Stot P() Q()
end observables

begin reaction rules
  P() -> 0  k1
  Q() -> 0  k2
end reaction rules

end model

begin actions
  generate_network({overwrite=>1})
  simulate({method=>"ode",t_start=>0,t_end=>10,n_steps=>40,suffix=>"tc"})
end actions
